==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|music|uncountable}} The [[ability]] to identify a [[note]] by name on hearing it, or to [[re-create]] a specified note from memory, without the benefit of an externally provided [[reference]] [[pitch]].
# {{lb|en|figurative|uncountable}} By extension, a [[reliable]] [[innate]] sense of exactly what is true, [[appropriate]], or needed in a given particular situation.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2015|author=Sophia Nguyen|chapterurl=https://www.harvardmagazine.com/2015/08/mumblecores-maestro|chapter=Mumblecore's Maestro: The perfect pitch of filmmaker {{w|Andrew Bujalski}}|title={{w|Harvard Magazine}}|section=September-October 2015
|passage=Bujalski has '''perfect pitch''': an instinct for how language meanders, and the lacunae it circles around.}}
# {{lb|en|music|less common|countable|or|uncountable}} The exact pitch of a note, described by its [[frequency]] in [[vibrations]] per [[second]].

